The directory mirrors RoboDojo's layout, so it can serve as the root for paths such as
Assets/Robots/x5/X5A.urdf.

curobo.yml is kept byte-identical; it carries RoboDojo's absolute asset path
(/workspace/RoboDojo/Assets/Robots/x5), which auriga_xpl/planner.py rewrites in a
temporary copy at load time to <root>/Assets/Robots/x5 (root: this directory by default).

Requires cuRobo v2 at commit d17b54ce32cba095c0b000c4c58777075d11de0e (RoboDojo's
third_party/curobo pin, https://github.com/yuechen0614/curobo), installed by
policy/Auriga/install_planner.sh.

ARX X5 meshes (Assets/Robots/x5/meshes/, not committed)
  download_robot_meshes.sh (run by download_assets.sh) fetches them into Assets/Robots/x5/meshes/ and
  checks them against Assets/Robots/x5/meshes.sha256. They are used by the Auriga adapter for the
  robot_model manifest, gripper collision bounds and robot-mesh overlays; the URDF, robot_config.yml
  and curobo.yml above are shared by the planner, the calibration FK and the adapter. Nothing here is a
  task asset.

